## Mixed Exercises

### Problem 30

**Cleaning.**

The cost `aₙ`, in dollars, to clean `n` rooms is `aₙ = 50 + 25(n − 1)`. Write a recursive formula for the cost.

### Problem 31

**Savings.**

The balance `aₙ`, in dollars, at the beginning of year `n` is `a₁ = 500, aₙ = 1.05aₙ₋₁, n ≥ 2`. Write an explicit formula for the balance.

### Problem 32

**Use tools.**

In 2010, County A had 1.3 million people. Its largest factory produced 1700 million widgets per year. The population is projected to increase by 1.2% per year. Widget production is expected to increase by 10 million widgets per year.

a. Develop explicit formulas for the population and annual widget production, in millions, as functions of the number of years `n` after 2010.
b. The graph of `(1700 + 10x)/(1.3(1.012)ˣ)` shows annual widget production per person from 2010 to 2020. Here, `x` is the number of years after 2010. The next-highest widget-producing county produces widgets at a constant rate of 1200 widgets per person. Use a graphing calculator to extend the graph. Find the year when County A will no longer be the leader. Explain your result.

![Original County A graph](/curriculum/module-8-lesson-6/source-image-9.png)

Accessible graph description: The horizontal axis is Years After 2010. The prompt spans 0 through 10 years. The printed labels are 0, 2, 4, 6, and 8; the axis arrow continues past 8. The vertical axis is Widgets per Person. It has an axis break below 1150 and labels 1150, 1200, 1250, and 1300. A decreasing blue curve starts slightly above 1300 at year 0 and is near 1230 at year 10. A horizontal green line marks 1200 widgets per person.

