### Problem 36

**Structure.**

The Tower of Hanoi has three pegs and disks of different sizes. The disks start on the left peg. The largest disk is at the bottom. Move the stack to the right peg. Follow all three rules: move only one disk at a time; move only the top disk on a peg; and never put a larger disk on a smaller disk.

![Original Tower of Hanoi diagram](/curriculum/module-8-lesson-6/source-image-11.png)

a. If `aₙ` is the number of moves for `n` disks, explain why `aₙ = aₙ₋₁ + 1 + aₙ₋₁` makes sense.
b. Simplify the recursive formula. What is `a₁`? Explain why.

